meta {
  name: Import Site Admin Templates
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/radiology-tests/import
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "masterDataId": "{{masterDataId}}",
    "templateIds": ["{{siteAdminRadiologyTestId}}"]
  }
}

docs {
  Bulk-import SITE_ADMIN radiology-test templates into the caller's master data.
  Business JWT. `tenantId`/`branchId` come from the JWT + the target master data;
  the body carries only `masterDataId` and `templateIds` (1..500, unique UUIDs).

  Each template is imported in its own transaction (one failure never aborts the
  batch) and deep-copied like Clone (fresh UUID, `source = "TENANT"`,
  `clonedFromId = template.id`, fresh `versionHistory` v1). Returns a summary:

  `{ "imported": [{templateId,radiologyTestId,testName}],
     "skipped":  [{templateId,testName,reason}],   // already imported here
     "failed":   [{templateId,testName,reason}] }`  // e.g. name/code conflict

  - `masterDataId` must belong to the caller's tenant → else 404
    `MASTER_DATA_NOT_FOUND`.
  - Templates already imported into this master data (`clonedFromId`) are skipped
    (idempotent re-import).
}
